    {
      "id": "a321be7507da4d41",
      "role": "B",
      "mission": {
        "base_commit": "98cc6b0c074c6fa129e78e62f2db915e95256795",
        "delegation_parent": "R/B",
        "depth": 1,
        "epoch": 1,
        "hypothesis": "Removing repeated container copies from the nested Prim and path-search loops, while expressing the minimum-key selection as a value reduction followed by a first-index lookup, may reduce memory traffic and expose a portable reduction loop to compiler auto-vectorization on the ARM64 target without changing traversal or tie-breaking behavior.",
        "id": "a321be7507da4d41",
        "ordinal": 1,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "B",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
        "transformations": {
          "files": [
            "src/tropical.cpp"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Pass read-only graph, edge, matrix, and search inputs by const reference to avoid repeatedly copying large vectors and matrices.",
            "Replace Prim's packed vector<bool> membership flags with contiguous byte flags; split min-key selection into a minimum-value reduction and a second scan for the first matching eligible index, preserving tie behavior.",
            "Reuse the recursive path vector as a push/pop stack and pass the graph by const reference, restoring the path on unsuccessful branches while avoiding repeated path and graph copies."
          ]
        },
        "tree_id": "e1:B",
        "trial_id": "01M53TQ64GYCHG22VMZM92ATBN",
